text:
To turn this mock-up into a colorful and interactive website, you would need to create a combination of HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. 

1. First, create a container to hold the website's content, which is currently in a series of boxes. Use HTML `div` elements to wrap the content, and add some CSS styling for better appearance.
```html
<div class="main">
    <div class="my-joke">My Joke Website</div>
    <div class="funny-joke">Funny Joke</div>
    <div class="reveal-punchline">Push to Reveal Punchline?</div>
</div>
```
1. Create a JavaScript function that listens for the `push to reveal punchline` button's click.
```javascript
const pushToRevealButton = document.querySelector('.reveal-punchline');
pushToRevealButton.addEventListener('click', () => {
    const funnyJoke = document.querySelector('.funny-joke').textContent;
    document.querySelector('.main').textContent = funnyJoke;
});
```
1. Create a joke database and use JavaScript to fetch random jokes from it. Store the jokes in an array and use the array to update the `funny-joke` div's text.
```javascript
const jokeDatabase = [
    { joke: "I'm reading this book on the history of glue.", author: "Dave Barry" },
    { joke: "I'm reading this book on the history of glue.", author: "Dave Barry" },
    // ... add more jokes
];

function fetchRandomJoke() {
    const randomJokeIndex = Math.floor(Math.random() * jokeDatabase.length);
    const randomJoke = jokeDatabase[randomJokeIndex];
    document.querySelector('.funny-joke').textContent = randomJoke.joke;
}

fetchRandomJoke();
setInterval(fetchRandomJoke, 60000); // Update joke every 60 seconds
```
